# Slice 307 (CALL-WHOLE-ARGUMENTS-STRUCTURE; the author's answer of 2026-11-08, LMX_blog/2026-11-08.md): a call with one
# Structure argument to which two readings apply -- the Structure is the one argument (the first formal a Structure formal
# the Structure fits by the first part of implements, every other formal defaulted), and its fields are the arguments
# (every field names a formal) -- is ambiguous and is refused at translation.  k (Q: q; int: z 0) given QZ (int: z 5; Q: q):
# QZ fits q (k reads q\z, QZ has z) and its fields z, q are k's formals.
Q:
    int: z 1
end: Q
QZ:
    int: z 5
    Q: q
end: QZ
fn: k (Q: q; int: z 0) int
    return: q\z * 10 + z
end: k
fn: run () int
    return: k(QZ)
end: run
int: code run()
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: code; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
